IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `era-types`
IMPORT `era-periods`
IMPORT `era-notice`

-- Employment Rights Act 1996 (UK) — GOAL 2: UNFAIR DISMISSAL.
--
--   "Can the employee complain of unfair dismissal, by when must the
--    complaint be presented, and what is the basic award?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1996-18.txt — ss 95, 108, 111,
-- 119-122, 207B, 227.

§ `Goal 2 — unfair dismissal`

-- s 95(1): the employee is dismissed if "(a) the contract under which he is
-- employed is terminated by the employer (whether with or without notice),
-- (b) he is employed under a limited-term contract and that contract
-- terminates by virtue of the limiting event without being renewed under the
-- same contract, or (c) the employee terminates the contract ... in
-- circumstances in which he is entitled to terminate it without notice by
-- reason of the employer's conduct."
@ref s 95(1)
GIVEN t IS A `Termination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is dismissed under s 95(1) by` t IF
    CONSIDER t's `how it ended`
    WHEN `terminated by the employee otherwise` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 108(1) "Section 94 does not apply to the dismissal of an employee unless
-- he has been continuously employed for a period of not less than two years
-- ending with the effective date of termination." (2): one month in a
-- s 64(2) case. (3)-(5): (1) does not apply for the listed reasons.
@ref s 108(1)-(5)
@export Whether the qualifying period in s 108 of the Employment Rights Act 1996 (UK) is met: continuous employment of two years ending with the effective date of termination (extended under s 97(2) or (4)); one month where the dismissal is for a s 64(2) requirement; no period where s 108(3)-(5) applies. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`               @desc The day continuous employment began
      t   IS A `Termination`             @desc How and when the contract ended
      u   IS AN `Unfair dismissal facts` @desc Whether a s 64(2) or s 108(3)-(5) reason applies
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the qualifying period in s 108 is met by` emp `for` t `with` u IF
    BRANCH
        IF   u's `a reason needing no qualifying period` THEN TRUE
        IF   u's `dismissed for a s 64(2) requirement`  THEN emp `has been continuously employed for` 1 `months ending with` edt
        OTHERWISE emp `has been continuously employed for` 24 `months ending with` edt
    WHERE
        edt MEANS `the effective date of termination for ss 108(1) and 119(1) of` emp `and` t

-- s 111(2) "an employment tribunal shall not consider a complaint under this
-- section unless it is presented to the tribunal— (a) before the end of the
-- period of three months beginning with the effective date of termination".
-- (2A): s 207B applies for (2)(a). The effective date of termination here is
-- the one in s 97(1); s 97(2) extends it only for ss 108(1), 119(1), 227(3).
@ref s 111(2)(a), (2A), s 207B
@export The last day to present a complaint of unfair dismissal under s 111(2)(a) of the Employment Rights Act 1996 (UK): the last day of the three months beginning with the effective date of termination, extended for early conciliation under s 207B. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Termination`             @desc The day the contract ended
      u IS AN `Unfair dismissal facts` @desc Early conciliation Day A and Day B, if any
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to present an unfair dismissal complaint for` t `with` u MEANS
    `the time limit` (`the last day of the` 3 `months beginning with` edt) `of the period beginning with` edt `extended under s 207B by` (u's `early conciliation`)
    WHERE
        edt MEANS `the effective date of termination under s 97(1) of` t

-- s 111(2)-(3): a complaint in time, one the tribunal allows under (2)(b),
-- or, where the dismissal is with notice, one "presented after the notice is
-- given but before the effective date of termination".
@ref s 111(2)-(3)
GIVEN t IS A `Termination`, u IS AN `Unfair dismissal facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tribunal may consider the unfair dismissal complaint for` t `with` u IF
    CONSIDER u's `complaint presented on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST p  THEN
            p AT MOST `the last day to present an unfair dismissal complaint for` t `with` u
        OR  u's `late complaint allowed`
        OR  withNotice p
    WHERE
        GIVEN p IS A DATE
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        withNotice p MEANS
            CONSIDER t's `notice given on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST n  THEN p AT LEAST n AND p LESS THAN t's `ended on`

§§ `The basic award (ss 119-122)`

-- s 119(1)-(3), with a week's pay capped by s 227(1)(a), over the period
-- ending with the effective date of termination (extended by s 97(2)/(4)).
@ref s 119, s 227(1)(a)
GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, t IS A `Termination`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 119 amount for` emp `and` t MEANS
        `the weeks' pay for the years of employment of` emp `ending with` (`the effective date of termination for ss 108(1) and 119(1) of` emp `and` t)
    TIMES `a week's pay, capped under s 227(1), for` emp

-- s 120(1) "The amount of the basic award (before any reduction under
-- section 122) shall not be less than £9,157 where the reason ... is one of
-- those specified in section 100(1)(a) and (b), 101A(d), 102(1) or 103."
-- (1C): not less than £5,000 for a s 104F (blacklist) dismissal. s 121: "The
-- amount of the basic award shall be two weeks' pay where" the reason is
-- redundancy and s 138 or s 141 applies.
@ref ss 119-121
GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, t IS A `Termination`, u IS AN `Unfair dismissal facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic award before reductions for` emp `and` t `with` u MEANS
    CONSIDER u's `reason`
    WHEN `a reason listed in s 120(1)`      THEN `the greater of` s119 9157
    WHEN `a blacklist reason under s 104F`  THEN `the greater of` s119 5000
    WHEN `redundancy, within s 121`         THEN 2 TIMES `a week's pay, capped under s 227(1), for` emp
    OTHERWISE s119
    WHERE
        s119 MEANS `the s 119 amount for` emp `and` t

-- s 122(1)-(3A): reductions the tribunal considers just and equitable (an
-- input). s 122(4) "The amount of the basic award shall be reduced or further
-- reduced by the amount of— (a) any redundancy payment awarded by the
-- tribunal under Part XI in respect of the same dismissal, or (b) any payment
-- made by the employer to the employee on the ground that the dismissal was
-- by reason of redundancy". Not below nothing.
@ref ss 119-122, 227(1)(a)
@export The basic award of compensation for unfair dismissal under ss 119-122 of the Employment Rights Act 1996 (UK): for each year of continuous employment (up to twenty, counted back from the effective date of termination) one and a half, one or half a week's pay by age, a week's pay capped at £751; at least £9,157 for a s 120(1) reason or £5,000 for a s 104F reason; two weeks' pay in a s 121 case; less the tribunal's just and equitable reductions and any redundancy payment for the same dismissal. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`               @desc Date of birth, the day continuous employment began, and a week's pay
      t   IS A `Termination`             @desc How and when the contract ended
      u   IS AN `Unfair dismissal facts` @desc The reason for dismissal, the tribunal's reductions and any redundancy payment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic award for` emp `and` t `with` u MEANS
    `the greater of` 0
        (    `the basic award before reductions for` emp `and` t `with` u
       MINUS u's `just and equitable reductions`
       MINUS u's `redundancy payments for the same dismissal`)

-- The answer for the goal: the basic award, where the employee was
-- dismissed, meets the qualifying period, presented a complaint the tribunal
-- may consider, and the dismissal was found unfair; otherwise 0.
@ref ss 94, 108, 111, 112(4), 119-122
GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, t IS A `Termination`, u IS AN `Unfair dismissal facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic award awarded to` emp `for` t `with` u MEANS
    IF       `the employee is dismissed under s 95(1) by` t
         AND `the qualifying period in s 108 is met by` emp `for` t `with` u
         AND `the tribunal may consider the unfair dismissal complaint for` t `with` u
         AND u's `found unfair`
    THEN `the basic award for` emp `and` t `with` u
    ELSE 0
